# builtin-is-contractive returns true for TypeNode.Union where all children are guarding.
# Case 3: Union/Intersect recurse into their `types` Seq. Each child is checked.
# A plain Int value (or any non-Union/Intersect/RecursiveRef value) is guarding — Case 2.
# If ALL children of a Union/Intersect are guarding, the Union as a whole is contractive.
#
# This represents μa.(Int | {val: a}) where the Record wrapper around a shields the
# recursive position — the Union's Int branch is also trivially guarding.
# Since no child of this Union is a bare RecursiveRef, the result is true.
[int-node:   42]
[union-node: [builtin-variant "TypeNode.Union" [types: [0: int-node]]]]
[result:     [builtin-is-contractive union-node]]
